            {
              "type": "reasoning.summary",
              "summary": "**Evaluating SSD1306 connections**\n\nI'm analyzing the SSD1306 pin configuration and focusing on U4 pin 28, which is supposed to be VCC. According to the spec, this pin seems to act as a supply pin, but it's isolated except for the capacitor C7 to GND. The datasheet confirms that pin 28 is indeed a supply pin. I wonder if the output from an internal DC/DC converter really operates at VCC. C7's role between VCC and ground appears typical in this context, suggesting all is as expected.**Examining VBAT connections**\n\nI've noticed that VBAT is tied to the VCC rail and VDD, but U2 pin 1 (VBAT) is left unconnected. I find it important to confirm whether the STM32L476\u2019s VBAT pin can indeed float. The datasheet states that if there's no external battery, VBAT should connect to VDD for RTC backup. It's a clear oversight that U2 pin 1 is unconnected. This setup likely impacts the MCU's functionality, since VBAT powers only the backup domain, but the core can still run if disconnected.",
